KosmicKrisp: a descriptor is initialized once, not twice

[[MTL4RenderPassDescriptor new] init] (and the argument-table, commit-options,
stencil and depth-stencil descriptors) ran -init on an object -new had already
initialized. MTL4RenderPassDescriptor's second init replaces its colour
attachment array without releasing the first: one
MTLRenderPassColorAttachmentDescriptorArrayInternal (96 bytes) leaked per
render pass -- 2.25 million of them, 215 MB, after four minutes of
Counter-Strike 2 (heap of the game's process, stage 61), growing for as long
as the game runs on a 16 GB machine that is already compressing memory.
Measured in isolation: 200000 [[new] init] descriptors +19 MB of footprint,
200000 [new] +128 KB.

--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_argument_table.m
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_argument_table.m
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 mtl_new_argument_table_descriptor()
 {
    @autoreleasepool {
-      return [[MTL4ArgumentTableDescriptor new] init];
+      return [MTL4ArgumentTableDescriptor new];
    }
 }
 
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_command_queue.m
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_command_queue.m
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
